+++ b/changelog/9358.bugfix.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+Fixed the source code shown in tracebacks for ``assert`` statements followed by a
+decorated function or class: the decorator (e.g. ``@t``) is no longer shown as
+part of the preceding statement. This restores the behavior from Python 3.7,
+since Python 3.8 changed the ``lineno`` of decorated definitions to point at the
+``def``/``class`` line rather than the first decorator.
